# Story 13.1 — the file-sanity harness writes transient files into
# disk/a/ during `make test-file-sanity`; a clean run deletes them at
# the end, but failed runs may leave stragglers. .gitkeep preserves
# the directory itself for iz-cpm's --disk-a mapping (AC #8).
disk/a/*.TXT
disk/a/*.BIN
# Story 13.2 — disk/b/ wired as iz-cpm's drive B: for the
# drive-routing probe (t8). Same transient-output convention.
disk/b/*.TXT
disk/b/*.BIN
# Story 18.5.1 code-review cleanup — tests/file_access_tests.fth lines
# 82..89 exercise the FCB-pool-exhaustion path by CREATE-FILE'ing
# P1.TXT..P8.TXT in the iz-cpm root (= repo root). Each run leaves
# zero-byte artifacts in the working tree; ignore them at the root.
/P[1-8].TXT
# Phase 6 HW-smoke — S9 verification on real MicroBeast dumps a serial
# capture (beastty-<timestamp>.bin) next to the story records. These are
# archived out-of-repo per story Change Logs, never committed as blobs.
_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/beastty-*.bin
